{"format":"vetro-plugin","version":1,"manifest":{"id":"shell","name":"Shell","version":"1.0.0","apiVersion":1,"permissions":["exec"],"main":"index.js","ui":{"label":"Shell"},"description":"A root shell on the TV from the dashboard, one command at a time; cd is remembered.","author":"piecifra"},"files":{"README.md":"# Shell\n\nA root shell on the TV, on a page in the Vetro dashboard, laid out like a terminal: the prompt sits under the output\nand each command stays in the scrollback with what it printed. One command at a time; `cd` is remembered between\ncommands, history is kept, and each command has a time limit you choose (10–120 s).\n\nKeys: Enter runs · ↑ ↓ history · Ctrl+C drops the line you are typing · Ctrl+U clears it · Ctrl+L or `clear`\nclears the screen. Ctrl+C does not stop a command that is already running: the time limit does.\n\nIt is the dashboard counterpart of Vetro's `POST /exec`, with bounded input and a working directory. Only paired\ndevices can open it, like the rest of Vetro.\n\n## Permissions\n\n`exec`: running the commands you type is the whole point of this Shard.\n\n## Commands it runs\n\n| Command | Why |\n| --- | --- |\n| **the command you type**, exactly as typed | that is what a shell does; nothing runs unless you press Enter |\n| a wrapper around it: `cd '<cwd>'`, then your command, then `printf` of the directory it ended in | to carry the working directory over to the next command |\n\nHow a command is run, so you can check it in `index.js` (`build()`):\n\n- It travels base64-encoded and runs in a fresh `bash` (or `sh` when the TV has no bash), with stdin on\n  `/dev/null`, so a command that waits for input ends instead of holding Vetro's command queue.\n- The directory comes back after a marker line carrying a random per-request nonce, so a command's own output\n  cannot fake it.\n- Limits: command 16 KB, output 256 KB (marked as cut), time limit 1–120 s (default 30 s). One command at a time;\n  other Vetro actions wait while it runs.\n- Programs that need a terminal or keyboard input (`vi`, `top`, `less`) do not work: use `top -b -n 1`, `cat`, …\n  Variables and aliases are not kept between commands.\n\nThe Shard runs nothing by itself: no timer, no command at start.\n\n**A command typed here runs as root and can damage the TV's system.** Read it before you run it.\n\n## Network\n\nNone. The page talks only to its own routes on the TV (`run`, `state`, `history`).\n\n## Data it keeps\n\nIts own `config.json` on the TV: the last 200 commands you ran (shown with ↑ ↓) and the last working directory.\n`DELETE history` (or removing the Shard) clears them.\n\n## Tested\n\nSamsung TV with Tizen 6.5 (kernel 5.4, ARMv7), Vetro 0.5.0, installed from a file: commands run as uid 0 in\nbash 3.2.57, `cd /opt/... && ls` carried the directory over, stderr and exit codes shown, `cat` returned at once with\nstdin closed. Also tested off the TV inside Vetro 0.5.0's plugin host, and on a local shell for odd directory names\n(quotes, `$()`), exit codes and a spoofed marker.\n","index.js":"'use strict';\n// Shell: runs one command at a time on the TV as root (ctx.execute, the same path as Vetro's own commands).\n// Each command gets a fresh shell, so only the working directory is carried over: the command runs in the cwd the\n// page sends, and the cwd it ends in comes back after a marker line with a per-request nonce (a command cannot\n// fake it). bash is used when the TV has it, sh otherwise. stdin is /dev/null so a command waiting for input ends\n// instead of holding Vetro's command queue until the time limit. Plain ES5: older TVs run Node 4.4.\nvar crypto = require('crypto'), fs = require('fs'), path = require('path');\nvar DEFAULT_TIMEOUT = 30000, MAX_TIMEOUT = 120000, MAX_COMMAND = 16384, MAX_OUTPUT = 262144, MAX_HISTORY = 200, MAX_BODY = 32768;\n\n// Node 4.4 has a Buffer.from inherited from Uint8Array that does not take a string; Node 5.10+ has the real one.\nfunction bytes(s) { return Buffer.from && Buffer.from !== Uint8Array.from ? Buffer.from(s) : new Buffer(s); }\nfunction quote(s) { return \"'\" + String(s).replace(/'/g, \"'\\\\''\") + \"'\"; }\nfunction validCwd(cwd) { return typeof cwd === 'string' && cwd.charAt(0) === '/' && cwd.length <= 4096 && !/[\\0\\n\\r]/.test(cwd); }\n\nfunction build(p) {\n    p = p || {};\n    var cmd = p.cmd, cwd = p.cwd == null ? '/' : p.cwd, timeout = p.timeout == null ? DEFAULT_TIMEOUT : p.timeout;\n    if (typeof cmd !== 'string' || !cmd.trim()) throw new Error('Missing command');\n    if (cmd.length > MAX_COMMAND) throw new Error('Command too long');\n    if (!validCwd(cwd)) throw new Error('Invalid working directory');\n    if (typeof timeout !== 'number' || !(timeout >= 1000) || timeout > MAX_TIMEOUT) throw new Error('Time limit must be 1–120 seconds');\n    var nonce = crypto.randomBytes(8).toString('hex'), marker = '__VETRO_CWD_' + nonce + '__';\n    var shown = cwd.replace(/[^\\x20-\\x7e]/g, '?').replace(/[\"$`\\\\]/g, '?');\n    var script = 'cd ' + quote(cwd) + ' 2>/dev/null || { echo \"cd: ' + shown + ': not found, using /\" >&2; cd /; }\\n' +\n        cmd + '\\n__vetro_status=$?\\nprintf \"\\\\n' + marker + '%s\\\\n\" \"$(pwd)\"\\nexit $__vetro_status\\n';\n    var b64 = bytes(script).toString('base64');\n    var command = '__vetro_script=\"$(echo ' + b64 + ' | base64 -d)\"; if command -v bash >/dev/null 2>&1; then exec bash -c \"$__vetro_script\" </dev/null; else exec sh -c \"$__vetro_script\" </dev/null; fi';\n    return { command: command, nonce: nonce, timeout: Math.round(timeout), cwd: cwd };\n}\n\nfunction cap(s) { s = String(s || ''); return s.length > MAX_OUTPUT ? { text: s.slice(0, MAX_OUTPUT), truncated: true } : { text: s, truncated: false }; }\n\nfunction parse(r, job) {\n    r = r || {};\n    var out = String(r.stdout || ''), marker = '\\n__VETRO_CWD_' + job.nonce + '__', i = out.lastIndexOf(marker), cwd = job.cwd;\n    if (i >= 0) {\n        var rest = out.slice(i + marker.length), nl = rest.indexOf('\\n'), found = nl < 0 ? rest : rest.slice(0, nl);\n        if (validCwd(found)) cwd = found;\n        out = out.slice(0, i) + rest.slice(nl < 0 ? rest.length : nl + 1);\n    }\n    var so = cap(out), se = cap(r.stderr);\n    return { ok: r.exit_code === 0 && !r.timed_out, exit_code: r.exit_code, timed_out: !!r.timed_out, stdout: so.text, stderr: se.text, truncated: so.truncated || se.truncated, cwd: cwd };\n}\n\nfunction run(execute, p) {\n    var job;\n    try { job = build(p); } catch (e) { return Promise.reject(e); }\n    return execute(job.command, job.timeout).then(function (r) { return parse(r, job); });\n}\n\nfunction json(res, body, code) {\n    res.writeHead(code || 200, { 'content-type': 'application/json', 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\n    res.end(JSON.stringify(body));\n}\nfunction readJson(req, cb) {\n    var chunks = [], size = 0, done = false;\n    req.on('data', function (c) { size += c.length; if (size > MAX_BODY) { if (!done) { done = true; cb(new Error('Request too large')); } req.destroy && req.destroy(); return; } chunks.push(c); });\n    req.on('end', function () { if (done) return; done = true; var p; try { p = JSON.parse(Buffer.concat(chunks).toString('utf8') || '{}'); } catch (e) { return cb(new Error('Invalid JSON')); } if (!p || typeof p !== 'object' || Array.isArray(p)) return cb(new Error('Invalid JSON')); cb(null, p); });\n    req.on('error', function (e) { if (!done) { done = true; cb(e); } });\n}\n\nmodule.exports = function (ctx) {\n    var page = null, busy = false, runs = 0, lastCwd = '/';\n    function history() { var h = ctx.config.get().history; return Array.isArray(h) ? h.filter(function (x) { return typeof x === 'string'; }) : []; }\n    function remember(cmd, cwd) {\n        var c = ctx.config.get(), h = history();\n        if (h[h.length - 1] !== cmd) h.push(cmd);\n        c.history = h.slice(-MAX_HISTORY); c.cwd = cwd;\n        try { ctx.config.set(c); } catch (e) { /* history is a convenience */ }\n    }\n    return {\n        start: function () { page = fs.readFileSync(path.join(ctx.dir, 'ui.html'), 'utf8'); lastCwd = validCwd(ctx.config.get().cwd) ? ctx.config.get().cwd : '/'; },\n        stop: function () { page = null; },\n        status: function () { return { commands: runs, cwd: lastCwd, running: busy }; },\n        route: function (req, res, sub) {\n            if (sub === 'ui' && req.method === 'GET') {\n                res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8', 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\n                res.end(page || '');\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'state' && req.method === 'GET') { json(res, { cwd: lastCwd, history: history(), busy: busy }); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'history' && req.method === 'DELETE') { var c = ctx.config.get(); c.history = []; ctx.config.set(c); json(res, { ok: true }); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'run' && req.method === 'POST') {\n                readJson(req, function (err, p) {\n                    if (err) return json(res, { ok: false, error: err.message }, 400);\n                    if (busy) return json(res, { ok: false, error: 'A command is already running' }, 409);\n                    try { build(p); } catch (e) { return json(res, { ok: false, error: e.message }, 400); }\n                    busy = true;\n                    run(ctx.execute, p).then(function (d) {\n                        runs++; lastCwd = d.cwd; remember(p.cmd, d.cwd); json(res, d);\n                    }, function (e) {\n                        json(res, { ok: false, error: String(e && e.message || e) }, 503);\n                    }).then(function () { busy = false; }, function () { busy = false; });\n                });\n                return true;\n            }\n            return false;\n        }\n    };\n};\nmodule.exports.build = build;\nmodule.exports.parse = parse;\nmodule.exports.run = run;\n","ui.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\"><title>Shell</title>\n<style>\n:root{--bg:#080f23;--term:#050a18;--border:#344360;--text:#e6ecfa;--muted:#aab8d1;--prompt:#8fbaff;--danger:#ef8a80;--mono:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme:light){:root{--bg:#f5f8ff;--term:#ffffff;--border:#c9d3e6;--text:#0b1430;--muted:#4a5878;--prompt:#123bb5;--danger:#b3261e}}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}html,body{height:100%}\nbody{margin:0;padding:12px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);font:14px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px}\n.bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:8px;color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}\n.bar .info{flex:1;min-width:200px}.bar code{font-family:var(--mono)}\nbutton,select{height:30px;padding:0 10px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;background:transparent;color:inherit;font:inherit;cursor:pointer}\n#term{flex:1;min-height:320px;overflow:auto;padding:10px 12px;background:var(--term);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;\n font:13px/1.45 var(--mono);white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-all;cursor:text}\n#term:focus-within{border-color:var(--prompt)}\n.p{color:var(--prompt)}.err{color:var(--danger)}.note{color:var(--muted)}\n#line{display:flex;align-items:baseline}\n#line .p{white-space:pre;flex-shrink:0}\n#cmd{flex:1;min-width:2ch;margin:0;padding:0;border:0;outline:0;background:transparent;color:var(--text);font:inherit;caret-color:var(--prompt)}\n#line.busy #cmd{visibility:hidden}\n</style></head><body>\n<div class=\"bar\">\n <span class=\"info\">Root shell on the TV, one command at a time (bash if the TV has it). <code>cd</code> is remembered; variables are not. No <code>vi</code>/<code>top</code>/<code>less</code>: use <code>top -b -n 1</code>. A command here can damage the TV: read it before you run it.</span>\n <label>Time limit <select id=\"limit\"><option value=\"10\">10 s</option><option value=\"30\" selected>30 s</option><option value=\"60\">60 s</option><option value=\"120\">120 s</option></select></label>\n <button id=\"clear\" type=\"button\" title=\"Ctrl+L\">Clear</button>\n</div>\n<div id=\"term\" role=\"log\" aria-live=\"polite\" aria-label=\"Shell\"><div id=\"out\"></div><div id=\"line\"><span class=\"p\" id=\"prompt\">root@tv:/# </span><input id=\"cmd\" spellcheck=\"false\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Command\" autofocus></div></div>\n<script>\nvar cwd='/',busy=false,hist=[],pos=0,draft='',MAXNODES=2000;\nfunction $(id){return document.getElementById(id)}\nfunction ps1(){return 'root@tv:'+cwd+'# '}\nfunction prompt(){$('prompt').textContent=ps1()}\nfunction bottom(){var t=$('term');t.scrollTop=t.scrollHeight}\nfunction print(t,c){if(!t)return;var o=$('out'),s=document.createElement('span');if(c)s.className=c;s.textContent=t;o.appendChild(s);while(o.childNodes.length>MAXNODES)o.removeChild(o.firstChild);bottom()}\nfunction nl(t){return t&&t.charAt(t.length-1)!=='\\n'?t+'\\n':t}\nfunction api(u,b){return fetch(u,b===undefined?{}:{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify(b)}).then(function(r){return r.json().then(function(d){if(!r.ok&&d.stdout===undefined&&d.error)throw new Error(d.error);return d})})}\nfunction clear(){$('out').textContent='';$('cmd').focus()}\napi('state').then(function(d){cwd=d.cwd||'/';hist=d.history||[];pos=hist.length;prompt()}).catch(function(){prompt()});\nfunction run(cmd){\n // the prompt line becomes scrollback, as in a terminal\n print(ps1(),'p');print(cmd+'\\n');\n if(hist[hist.length-1]!==cmd&&cmd.trim())hist.push(cmd);pos=hist.length;draft='';\n if(!cmd.trim())return;\n if(cmd.trim()==='clear'){clear();return}\n busy=true;$('line').className='busy';$('prompt').textContent='';\n api('run',{cmd:cmd,cwd:cwd,timeout:Number($('limit').value)*1000}).then(function(d){\n  print(nl(d.stdout));print(nl(d.stderr),'err');\n  if(d.timed_out)print('[stopped after '+$('limit').value+' s: time limit]\\n','note');\n  if(d.truncated)print('[output cut at 256 KB]\\n','note');\n  if(d.cwd)cwd=d.cwd;\n }).catch(function(e){print('vetro: '+e.message+'\\n','err')}).then(function(){busy=false;$('line').className='';prompt();$('cmd').focus();bottom()})}\n$('cmd').onkeydown=function(e){\n if(e.key==='Enter'){e.preventDefault();if(busy)return;var c=this.value;this.value='';run(c)}\n else if(e.key==='ArrowUp'){e.preventDefault();if(pos===hist.length)draft=this.value;if(pos>0)this.value=hist[--pos]}\n else if(e.key==='ArrowDown'){e.preventDefault();if(pos<hist.length){pos++;this.value=pos===hist.length?draft:hist[pos]}}\n else if(e.ctrlKey&&(e.key==='l'||e.key==='L')){e.preventDefault();clear()}\n else if(e.ctrlKey&&(e.key==='c'||e.key==='C')&&!window.getSelection().toString()){e.preventDefault();if(busy)return;print(ps1(),'p');print(this.value+'^C\\n');this.value='';pos=hist.length}\n else if(e.ctrlKey&&(e.key==='u'||e.key==='U')){e.preventDefault();this.value=''}};\n// a click anywhere in the terminal types at the prompt, unless you are selecting text to copy\n$('term').onmouseup=function(){if(!window.getSelection().toString())$('cmd').focus()};\n$('clear').onclick=clear;\nprompt();\n</script></body></html>\n"}}
